  <keyword>ode object workflow tutorial</keyword>
  <short_description>Define and solve ODE problems with class objects.</short_description>
  <description>
    <p>The <b>ode</b> class stores a problem definition, including the equation, initial state, parameters, events, mass matrix, Jacobian, and solver options.</p>
    <table style="width:100%">
  <tr><th>Property</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
  <tr><td><b>ODEFcn</b>, <b>InitialValue</b></td><td>Define the differential equation and initial state.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>Solver</b>, <b>SolverOptions</b></td><td>Select the integration method and its options.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>EventDefinition</b>, <b>MassMatrix</b>, <b>Jacobian</b></td><td>Add zero crossing, mass matrix, or Jacobian information.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>Sensitivity</b>, <b>DelayDefinition</b></td><td>Add sensitivities or delayed states when supported by the selected workflow.</td></tr>
</table>
    <p>Call <b>solve</b> to obtain a result object, or <b>solutionFcn</b> to obtain an interpolation function together with the result object.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Create a reusable problem object.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[problem = ode('ODEFcn', @(t,y,rate) -rate * y, ...
  'InitialValue', 1, 'Parameters', {2});
result = solve(problem, 0, 1)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Use solutionFcn for interpolation.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[problem = ode('ODEFcn', @(t,y) -y, 'InitialValue', 1);
[f, result] = solutionFcn(problem, 0, 1);
f(0.5)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
